# MY MANDAT — AI advisor (Penasihat AI)
# Copy to .env.local and fill in your key to enable the live Claude-powered
# advisor at /advisor. Without a key the advisor runs in local simulation
# (rule-based) mode — the game remains fully playable.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# MY MANDAT — account login (/login, /register)
# Copy to .env.local and fill in your Supabase project's values to enable
# accounts. Find these under Project Settings > API in your Supabase
# dashboard. Without them, login/register is skipped entirely and the game
# is reachable directly, same local-fallback pattern as the advisor above.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

# MY MANDAT — in-app purchases (Stripe)
# Run supabase/migrations/20260806_purchases_and_premium.sql once (Supabase
# SQL Editor) before setting these. Without them, /api/checkout and
# /api/webhooks/stripe fail loudly rather than silently no-op, since a
# payment endpoint should never pretend to work when it can't actually
# charge anyone — see app/utils/stripe.ts.
#
# Server-only — NEVER exposed to the client, only used inside API routes.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# service_role key from Project Settings > API — DIFFERENT from
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY above. Bypasses Row Level Security
# entirely; only ever read inside app/utils/supabase/service.ts, which the
# Stripe webhook route uses because it has no user session to act as.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...
#
# Public — safe to expose client-side (Price IDs aren't secret, and
# @stripe/stripe-js is installed for future use, but the current checkout
# flow redirects to Stripe-hosted Checkout and doesn't need Stripe.js/
# Elements directly, so NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY isn't required
# yet — set it now anyway if you know you'll want embedded Elements later).
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# Real sandbox/test-mode Price IDs (not secret) — swap for your own if you
# create different test products, and swap again for the live-mode IDs
# before actually going live (test and live Price IDs are never the same).
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PRICE_PRN=price_...
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PRICE_PREMIUM_MONTHLY=price_...
